    {
      "paper_id": "doi:10.1016/j.jet.2026.106206",
      "sequence": 2,
      "source_sequence": 2,
      "article_type": "research-article",
      "title_en": "Investment sophistication and wealth inequality",
      "title_cn": "投资复杂度和财富不平等",
      "authors": [
        "Ehsan Azarmsa"
      ],
      "abstract_en": "I study how differences in investment sophistication, the ability to identify profitable investment opportunities, contribute to wealth inequality and its dynamics. I analyze a financial market with a continuum of investors heterogeneously informed about the distribution of future returns. The stationary distribution of wealth shares features a thick right tail populated by the best-informed investors. Wealth inequality increases with the emergence of ever-costlier information production technologies, but the expected excess return achieved through such technologies is bounded in the long run. Top wealth shares have an inverted U-shaped relationship with the wealth share delegated to the best-informed investors to manage. Empirically, wealthier households indeed tend to have more precise beliefs, and the gap in their beliefs can rationalize inequality under reasonable parameters. My findings suggest subsidizing education and leveling the playing field regarding information can help reduce inequality.",
      "abstract_cn": "我研究投资复杂程度的差异、识别有利可图的投资机会的能力如何导致财富不平等及其动态。我分析了一个金融市场，其中有一系列投资者对未来回报的分布有不同的了解。财富份额的平稳分布具有一条粗右尾，由最消息灵通的投资者占据。随着成本越来越高的信息生产技术的出现，财富不平等加剧，但从长远来看，通过此类技术实现的预期超额回报是有限的。顶级财富份额与委托给最了解情况的投资者管理的财富份额之间存在倒U形关系。从经验来看，较富裕的家庭确实往往有更精确的信念，而他们信念的差距可以在合理的参数下使不平等合理化。我的研究结果表明，补贴教育和创造公平的信息竞争环境有助于减少不平等。",
      "abstract_snippet_en": "",
